  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(d) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CsI</mi></math> salt is poor water soluble due to its low hydration energy.<br />(b) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaHCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is used in fire extinguisher.<br />(c) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is most abundant element in cell fluid.<br />(a) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> decomposes easily due to high covalent character caused by small size <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;cation.</p><p>Hence, option 1 is the best response.</p>",
